  "notes": "Every figure on this row is Ubiquiti's, read 2026-11-21. https://dl.ui.com/ds/usw-pro-24-poe_ds.pdf (HTTP 200, application/pdf, 443,168 B, 2 pp) prints 'Networking interface (24) GbE RJ45 ports / (2) 1/10G SFP+ ports', 'PoE interface (16) PoE/PoE+ (Pins 1, 2+; 3, 6-) / (8) 60W PoE++; PoE/PoE+ ...', 'Total available PoE 400W', 'Max PoE wattage per port by PSE PoE+: 32W / PoE++: 64W'. https://techspecs.ui.com/unifi/switching/usw-pro-24-poe (HTTP 200, 654,711 B, rendered spec table) prints the same counts as rows - '1 GbE RJ45 24 (16 PoE+; 8 PoE++) (1G/100M/10M)', '10G SFP+ 2 (10G/1G)', 'Total PoE Availability 400W', 'PoE Ports PoE+ 16 / PoE++ 8' - but a lower per-port row, 'PoE+ 30W / PoE++ 60W'. The two vendor surfaces disagree by 2 W per class (32/64 vs 30/60); this row uses the datasheet figures, the same ones the USW-Enterprise rows carry. Ubiquiti prints counts and never says which sockets: the 8 PoE++ sockets are modelled as Ports 17-24, the upper end of the single 24-port bank - the ordering this catalogue already applies to USW-Pro-Max-24-PoE (eth8-15 above eth0-7) - because leaving them undeclared was not neutral, it made all 24 sockets report a 15.4 W 802.3af ceiling. Before this correction no copper port on the row declared poeOut, so engine/media.js's undeclared-port default gave every socket the 802.3af ceiling of 15.4 W and web/faceplate.js printed 'PoE out 15.4 W' on sockets the datasheet rates 802.3at/802.3bt. The SFP+ cages are not PSE ports and stay undeclared."
